#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161783 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161991 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f203c9bf-7d12-56db-aafe-6639162eae93" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given Old Variables Through New Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "248c9a29-6698-5c8c-b674-0b0dc537edf0" :question/math-academy-id "e-8177" :question/problem "Given that ![](images/57/57718ef2e6ecd26138c4c6a1b817d1129ad95a7473bf2e7d1611fdc64391e5c8.png) express the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})= x_1^2-x_2^2\\,$ in terms of the components of $\\mathbf{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that  \n\n![](images/12/12e6df2cc03a95228ac8d54512772c914f3283f1f62d814f2e996de67c93a041.png)\n\ngives the following expressions for $x_1$ and $x_2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}-(2{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-4{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161784 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161992 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f2a5391-d8bb-5084-941a-bb787e8729f3" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given New Variables Through Old Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "1c199cdf-ca23-53e8-8b5d-1ba43c842d41" :question/math-academy-id "e-8178" :question/problem "Given that ![](images/30/309c32ea89b3e3216e79962d305ef2611eeb691342ae07f7659aff52c218c5b3.png) express the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})= x_1x_2+2x_2^2$ in terms of the components of $\\mathbf{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n![](images/7e/7ea02af91b7b066c7aafa293882f6e2f9f81256fe8b0a30f33f2f4403142d928.png) \n\ngives the following expressions for $y_1$ and $y_2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the second equation for $x_1$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for $x_1$ and $x_2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-{y}_{2})(-{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+2(-{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{1}^{2}+8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+8{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{y}_{1}^{2}+9{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+10{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161785 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161993 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "331cb610-6168-5161-b821-237c713dedaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form Given a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "4c239ba2-66c9-5170-8a5a-9f7071315dd2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8179" :question/problem "Consider the matrices $A$ and $P$ below. Find the matrix of the quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$ \n\n![](images/8c/8c8f1626eafc81b4700a0ddc015c210508d4db464970abc706831ea86659e8da.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $\\mathbf{x}=[x_1, x_2]^T$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $\\mathbf{y}=[ y_1, y_2 ]^T$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = P\\mathbf{y}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161993 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "331cb610-6168-5161-b821-237c713dedaa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form Given a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2932a4-b77d-5037-8b7a-5ad4984405e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269976} {:answer/id #uuid "62798c61-83b7-5908-a0c2-44bda8e3e2f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270138} {:answer/id #uuid "7628b69e-00c7-5f88-9e3e-e446fe5e78d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270313} {:answer/id #uuid "92d8acbe-9445-5295-ac21-6c99210ccc69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270552} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a24b7c-da9c-51e8-8c36-9067d466db61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7628b69e-00c7-5f88-9e3e-e446fe5e78d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270313} :answer-field/id #uuid "070615ae-f175-5e5e-893e-c59d5f0fcf92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5a5ddb8-1d6f-5786-b73c-065c764a2c41" :question/math-academy-id "q-140941" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161991 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f203c9bf-7d12-56db-aafe-6639162eae93" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given Old Variables Through New Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5382892-cd2b-5a24-91be-e85cdae44939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 3y_{1}y_{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160899} {:answer/id #uuid "0e8facba-e8e6-56f3-8f84-0057a8ad261d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} + y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160900} {:answer/id #uuid "13b3d32d-5baa-5dc9-a066-1826a15f1be6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 7y_{1}y_{2} + 11y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160901} {:answer/id #uuid "18041767-5658-50b4-b48d-0d12b91a0bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 2y_{1}y_{2} - y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160902} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbac4b2-52ce-520f-9305-129bd8d9ac74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{1}^{2} - 3y_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160903}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4e7adc-5107-5de3-ad4d-7554ee71eefa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160898}] :question/id #uuid "21370042-e785-5cb0-bd56-e827bc7cef28" :question/math-academy-id "q-93733" :question/problem "Given that $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$, express the quadratic form $Q(x) = x_{1}^{2} - 3x_{1}x_{2} + x_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161991 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f203c9bf-7d12-56db-aafe-6639162eae93" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given Old Variables Through New Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0721553b-ff2a-510f-8bd9-315b27293eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354724} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6b2bc9-96e9-5a5d-a8a3-17638f361bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-8{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355018} {:answer/id #uuid "30306894-33d5-5826-bfe3-3cea878350e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355083} {:answer/id #uuid "79a9a162-4dfd-5acb-900f-43abaae30d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355730} {:answer/id #uuid "f040fb05-77e4-5612-b088-7ad0daf1999b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a6b2bc9-96e9-5a5d-a8a3-17638f361bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-8{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355018} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2adb9c2-ec4f-5c35-a39b-a01e94aab7b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de62870c-5c78-5d4e-9622-5e5ec12329c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-94123" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)=-{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  \n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-(2{y}_{1})^{2}+3(2{y}_{1})({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})-2({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =-4{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{1}^{2}+12{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{1}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-8{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-8{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161991 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f203c9bf-7d12-56db-aafe-6639162eae93" :knowledge-point/title "Changing Variables in a Quadratic Form Given Old Variables Through New Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1556ee77-a810-5153-a388-ba23b53930a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25{y}_{1}^{2}-9{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354854} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ca0917-6dad-5cd7-9d15-eabece4c0311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}_{1}^{2}-10{y}_{1}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356160} {:answer/id #uuid "aac69a34-b9fe-50ec-8264-65b0d070f036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25{y}_{1}^{2}+10{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356177} {:answer/id #uuid "b73f995e-c3ec-555e-8fe4-a2d886d2723f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/r